ADR refs    : ADR-002, ADR-004, ADR-005, ADR-006, ADR-011, ADR-013, ADR-014, ADR-015
Runner      : .NET 10.0.300 SDK present (dotnet --version 10.0.300) — NOT blocked.
Output      : apps/windows/TeslaSync.App/feature-views/EfficiencyPage/{EfficiencyPage.Model.cs,
              EfficiencyPage.Source.cs, EfficiencyPage.ViewModel.cs, EfficiencyPage.cs}
              (the generated prompt's idealized "TeslaSync/Features/Driving/EfficiencyPage.xaml +
              EfficiencyPageViewModel.cs" is mapped onto the repo's real code-first WinUI conventions —
              every sibling W7 page, e.g. BatteryDegradationPage / CostAnalysisPage / ProjectedRangePage,
              uses the same Model/Source/ViewModel/View C# quad, not .xaml page files).

=== APPROACH ===
- Code-first WinUI surface under apps/windows/TeslaSync.App/feature-views/EfficiencyPage/, namespace
  TeslaSync.App.FeatureViews.Driving. EfficiencyPage.Model.cs (pure, Microsoft.UI-free: records + tolerant
  JSON parsers + the EfficiencyProjection + EfficiencyStrings(42) + Registration + Diagnostics), .Source.cs
  (generated-client feed, Microsoft.UI-free), .ViewModel.cs (INotifyPropertyChanged + IDisposable holder),
  .cs (the Fluent view, a thin renderer). The three Microsoft.UI-free files are <Compile Include>-linked into
  TeslaSync.App.Tests so the projection/parsers/feed are verified headlessly (the established W7 pattern).
- Data sources — the web page's two hooks, bound through the generated OpenAPI client (ADR-004), scoped by the
  snake_case vehicle_id query param:
    * useDrivingStats -> GET /drives/stats (generated get_api_v1_drives_stats, Operations.Drives.Stats) — the
      PRIMARY read: a failure surfaces the page error state. Parsed by EfficiencyStats.FromJson (snake_case
      total_drives / total_distance_km / total_duration_s / avg_efficiency_wh_km / avg_speed_kmh /
      top_speed_kmh / regen_ratio / regen_energy_wh / co2_saved_kg, numeric-string tolerant).
    * useDrives -> GET /drives (generated get_api_v1_drives, Operations.Drives.List) — the SUPPLEMENTARY read
      powering the four charts + the temperature table; a failure degrades to an empty drive list (the web's
      two independent queries). Parsed by EfficiencySnapshot.ParseDrives (distance_m / start_ts / avg_speed_mps
      / outside_temp_avg_c / start_battery_pct / end_battery_pct). No HTTP touches the view.
- Projection (EfficiencyProjection.Project, EfficiencyPage.Model.cs) is the 1:1 port of the web page's useMemo
  aggregations + JSX: getEfficiency (battUsed*0.75*1000 / (distanceM/1000) Wh/km), the daily trend (first 30
  eff drives, reversed), the 0–30/30–60/60–90/90–120/120+ speed-range distribution, the speed/temperature
  scatter clouds (>3 points), the Celsius-bounded temperature buckets (labels localise to °C/°F), the hero
  gauge + km/kWh + CO₂ + total readouts, the four stat cards, the four summary metric bars and the six energy
  insights. Every branch / format / i18n happens here; the WinUI view binds the EfficiencyDisplay and renders.
- Units (P1/S5) — conversion happens ONLY at this display boundary, through the shared SI converters
  (UnitConverters.DistanceFromSi / SpeedFromSi / TemperatureFromSi) + formatters (ScalarFormatters.FormatNumber,
  UnitFormatters.FormatDuration / FormatEnergy). PARITY NOTE (honesty, ADR-006 "web is canonical"): the web page
  feeds those SI-from-meters / -mps converters the SAME inputs it does today — the real-SI drive fields
  (distance_m, avg_speed_mps, outside_temp_avg_c) AND the already-km/kmh stats fields (total_distance_km,
  avg_speed_kmh, top_speed_kmh), and it double-converts the temperature-bucket totals (EfficiencyPage.tsx L467,
  L473). Those expressions are replicated VERBATIM (cited in code comments) so the native render equals the
  canonical web output exactly; "fixing" the web's unit handling would be a backend/web change (out of scope) and
  a silent drift from the parity spec. Efficiency itself stays the web's Wh/km domain metric, converted to Wh/mi
  at the boundary (×1.609344).
- States — loading / empty / error / success, classified in Project's state ladder and rendered by the view
  (loading skeleton, TsQueryError retry surface, TsEmptyState page-empty, content host). Each in-content region
  ALSO carries its own empty fallback (hero/cards/summary/insights gate on stats; the four charts gate on drive
  counts via TsChartContainer.State=Empty; the temp table on bucket count) so no region renders blank (ADR-011).
- i18n (ADR-014) — every visible literal resolves through ILocalizer with the web key names. 38 of the 42
  efficiency.* keys already existed in Strings/{en,ar,he}/Resources.resw; the 4 chart aria keys
  (efficiency.dailyTrend.aria / speedDist.aria / speedVsEfficiency.aria / tempVsEfficiency.aria) were added to
  all three catalogs (the only catalog rows this change introduces).
- Nav — the "Efficiency" route (path "efficiency", group TripsDriving) already exists in RouteTable.cs; this
  change registers its page factory in ShellWindow.xaml.cs (_viewModel.PageFactory.Register("Efficiency", …)).
- a11y / theming (ADR-015) — AutomationProperties.SetName on the surface, every panel, each chart container
  (AccessibleSummary = the web aria-label), the table, the stat/insight tiles; brand colours come from design
  tokens (ChartRole brushes + TsColor*/TsChart* keys via DisplayTokens), so light/dark/high-contrast all flow
  from W1/W2. No hardcoded hex in the view.

